<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title><%= title %> — <%= appName %></title>
  <%- include('../_style') %>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1><%= title %></h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated <%= updatedAt %></p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Your name, email address and profile picture, as supplied by Google or Apple when you
      sign in. We never see or store a password, because there isn't one.
    </p>
    <p class="meaning">
      Your practice record: chanting rounds, daily targets, tasks, the struggles you report,
      and which verses you read. This is what the app is for, and it is what makes the
      personalised sloka possible.
    </p>
    <p class="meaning">
      Device information — model, operating system, app version and a push token — so
      notifications reach the right device.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do with it</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      We use it to run the app: to keep your practice record, to choose a verse for you, and
      to send the notifications you have asked for. Once a week we recompute what the app has
      learned about your preferences from your own activity.
    </p>
    <p class="meaning">
      We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>What you report about yourself</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      The struggles you record are private to your account. They are used to choose verses
      for you and to build your own report. They are never shown to anyone else, and they are
      not used to target advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>AI</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      The app uses AI to help write notes about verses and to connect verses to the struggles
      people report. That work happens in advance, over the scriptures themselves. Your
      personal practice record is not sent to an AI provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      You can delete your account from inside the app, under Settings. It is a real deletion:
      your practice history, favourites and notifications go with it, and it cannot be undone.
      See <a href="<%= webBaseUrl %>/account-deletion">account deletion</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Subscriptions and donations are processed by Google, Apple or Razorpay. We never see or
      store your card details. We keep a record of the amount, the currency and the date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Questions about any of this: <a href="mailto:privacy@hariharibol.com">privacy@hariharibol.com</a>
    </p>

    <footer class="muted"><p><%= appName %> &middot; <%= year %></p></footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
